WEBVTT

00:00:00.261 --> 00:00:03.391
Last video, we put one function inside another.

00:00:03.952 --> 00:00:06.236
Now let's multiply two of them, the way

00:00:06.257 --> 00:00:08.622
a deck's area is its length times its

00:00:08.703 --> 00:00:08.943
width.

00:00:09.826 --> 00:00:10.869
Here's e to the x,

00:00:11.552 --> 00:00:14.441
here's sine x, and here's their product, e

00:00:14.482 --> 00:00:15.665
to the x sine x.

00:00:16.369 --> 00:00:18.836
A quick guess for its derivative: just multiply

00:00:18.877 --> 00:00:19.619
the two derivatives.

00:00:20.082 --> 00:00:22.056
That gives e to the x times cos

00:00:22.117 --> 00:00:22.156
x.

00:00:23.104 --> 00:00:25.593
At pi over two, cos x is zero,

00:00:26.055 --> 00:00:27.962
so the guess says the curve is flat

00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:28.203
there.

00:00:28.867 --> 00:00:29.940
But look at the curve.

00:00:30.547 --> 00:00:32.856
At pi over two, it's climbing steeply.

00:00:33.619 --> 00:00:36.435
So how do both factors really contribute to

00:00:36.456 --> 00:00:36.897
the slope?

00:00:37.542 --> 00:00:38.830
Here's why that guess fails,

00:00:39.636 --> 00:00:40.179
with the deck.

00:00:40.621 --> 00:00:42.746
It's four metres long and two metres wide,

00:00:43.108 --> 00:00:44.852
so its area is eight square metres.

00:00:45.574 --> 00:00:47.759
While it's being built, its length grows by

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:49.804
one metre a day, and its width by

00:00:49.904 --> 00:00:50.766
half a metre a day.

00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:53.597
Multiply those two rates, and you'd guess the

00:00:53.757 --> 00:00:55.725
area grows by half a square metre a

00:00:55.745 --> 00:00:55.946
day.

00:00:56.631 --> 00:00:57.638
Now watch it grow.

00:00:58.361 --> 00:01:00.263
The extra length adds a strip down the

00:01:00.304 --> 00:01:01.645
side, two metres long:

00:01:02.327 --> 00:01:04.509
one metre a day, times two metres, is

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:05.671
two square metres a day.

00:01:06.413 --> 00:01:08.395
The extra width adds a strip along the

00:01:08.477 --> 00:01:09.878
top, four metres long:

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.422
half a metre a day, times four metres,

00:01:12.803 --> 00:01:14.365
is another two square metres a day.

00:01:15.086 --> 00:01:17.275
So right now, the area grows at four

00:01:17.336 --> 00:01:18.138
square metres a day,

00:01:18.642 --> 00:01:19.524
eight times the guess.

00:01:20.208 --> 00:01:22.355
Each side's growth is multiplied by the other

00:01:22.396 --> 00:01:23.118
side's size.

00:01:23.842 --> 00:01:24.668
Here's a way to see it.

00:01:25.291 --> 00:01:27.078
Think of the product as the area of

00:01:27.118 --> 00:01:29.345
a rectangle, with width e to the x

00:01:29.646 --> 00:01:30.991
and height sine x.

00:01:31.754 --> 00:01:34.002
At x equals one, it's about two point

00:01:34.023 --> 00:01:36.593
seven two wide, and point eight four high.

00:01:37.218 --> 00:01:38.572
Now nudge x a little.

00:01:39.258 --> 00:01:41.305
The width grows, and that adds a strip

00:01:41.347 --> 00:01:43.776
down the side: the change in width, times

00:01:43.797 --> 00:01:44.138
the height.

00:01:44.702 --> 00:01:46.749
The height grows too, adding a strip along

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.939
the top: the change in height, times the

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:49.160
width.

00:01:49.883 --> 00:01:52.207
The corner is a small change times a

00:01:52.228 --> 00:01:54.572
small change, so it vanishes as the nudge

00:01:54.613 --> 00:01:54.933
shrinks.

00:01:55.816 --> 00:01:57.860
So the area changes in two ways,

00:01:58.542 --> 00:02:00.326
one factor changing while the other stays.

00:02:01.007 --> 00:02:02.931
Divide by the nudge, and that's the product

00:02:02.972 --> 00:02:03.812
rule from Year 11:

00:02:04.375 --> 00:02:06.558
u prime v, plus u v prime.

00:02:07.261 --> 00:02:08.004
Back to the curve,

00:02:08.626 --> 00:02:09.629
at x equals one.

00:02:10.211 --> 00:02:12.236
E to the x's turn is its slope

00:02:12.316 --> 00:02:14.601
times the height of sine x, about two

00:02:14.641 --> 00:02:15.283
point two nine.

00:02:16.085 --> 00:02:18.152
Sine's turn is the height of e to

00:02:18.212 --> 00:02:20.159
the x times sine's slope,

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:21.844
about one point four seven.

00:02:22.687 --> 00:02:25.641
Together that's about three point seven six, the

00:02:25.662 --> 00:02:26.525
slope of the tangent.

00:02:27.351 --> 00:02:29.088
Now slide to pi over two.

00:02:29.793 --> 00:02:31.198
Sine x is at the top of its

00:02:31.219 --> 00:02:33.547
hump, so its slope is zero, and its

00:02:33.628 --> 00:02:34.591
turn is zero.

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:37.138
But e to the x is still growing,

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:39.384
and sine x is still one high,

00:02:40.007 --> 00:02:41.810
so e to the x's turn gives the

00:02:41.912 --> 00:02:44.157
whole slope, about four point eight one.

00:02:44.939 --> 00:02:47.251
The guess multiplied a slope by a slope,

00:02:47.594 --> 00:02:48.237
so it missed this.

00:02:48.896 --> 00:02:49.480
Keep sliding.

00:02:50.125 --> 00:02:52.766
Past pi over two, sine x starts to

00:02:52.847 --> 00:02:54.607
fall, so its slope is negative,

00:02:55.168 --> 00:02:57.668
and its turn pulls the slope down, while

00:02:57.689 --> 00:02:59.689
e to the x's turn still pushes it

00:02:59.791 --> 00:02:59.890
up.

00:03:00.792 --> 00:03:02.998
At three pi over four, the two turns

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.948
are equal and opposite, about plus and minus

00:03:06.069 --> 00:03:07.232
seven point four six.

00:03:07.936 --> 00:03:10.135
They cancel, so the tangent is flat.

00:03:10.838 --> 00:03:12.681
That's why this curve levels off at three

00:03:12.722 --> 00:03:15.066
pi over four, not at pi over two,

00:03:15.507 --> 00:03:16.589
where sine x levels off.

00:03:17.351 --> 00:03:19.262
E to the x is still growing, and

00:03:19.323 --> 00:03:20.851
it carries the product further.

00:03:21.536 --> 00:03:22.562
Now the algebra.

00:03:23.106 --> 00:03:25.693
Differentiate y equals e to the x sine

00:03:25.815 --> 00:03:25.934
x.

00:03:26.597 --> 00:03:27.568
Label the factors first.

00:03:28.378 --> 00:03:29.948
u is e to the x, so u

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.236
prime is e to the x.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:34.268
v is sine x, so v prime is

00:03:34.329 --> 00:03:34.710
cos x.

00:03:35.413 --> 00:03:37.720
Then u prime v, plus u v prime,

00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:40.209
gives e to the x sine x, plus

00:03:40.371 --> 00:03:41.594
e to the x cos x.

00:03:42.357 --> 00:03:44.340
Both terms share e to the x, so

00:03:44.381 --> 00:03:45.301
take it out as a factor:

00:03:45.863 --> 00:03:47.786
e to the x, times sine x plus

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:48.127
cos x.

00:03:48.932 --> 00:03:49.765
Check pi over two.

00:03:50.191 --> 00:03:52.077
That's e to the pi over two, times

00:03:52.299 --> 00:03:54.748
one plus zero, about four point eight one,

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:55.792
the slope we saw.

00:03:56.443 --> 00:03:57.918
The same rule works with a log.

00:03:58.422 --> 00:04:01.229
Differentiate y equals e to the x, times

00:04:01.269 --> 00:04:02.311
the natural log of x.

00:04:03.073 --> 00:04:05.699
The natural log needs x positive, so this

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.606
function only exists for x greater than zero.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.199
u is e to the x, and so

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:11.943
is u prime.

00:04:13.049 --> 00:04:14.834
v is the natural log of x, so

00:04:14.894 --> 00:04:16.659
v prime is one over x.

00:04:17.322 --> 00:04:19.049
That gives e to the x times the

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:20.818
natural log of x, plus e to the

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:21.621
x over x.

00:04:22.385 --> 00:04:23.987
Take out e to the x, and you

00:04:24.028 --> 00:04:25.850
get e to the x, times the natural

00:04:25.891 --> 00:04:28.014
log of x plus one over x, for

00:04:28.076 --> 00:04:28.716
positive x.

00:04:29.538 --> 00:04:31.325
Every new family works the same way:

00:04:31.849 --> 00:04:33.958
two turns, then look for a common factor.

00:04:34.629 --> 00:04:37.124
Next, a factor with a function inside.

00:04:37.648 --> 00:04:40.847
Differentiate y equals x cubed, sine two x.

00:04:41.572 --> 00:04:44.525
The outside operation is multiplication, so it's the

00:04:44.566 --> 00:04:45.067
product rule.

00:04:46.073 --> 00:04:48.405
u is x cubed, so u prime is

00:04:48.466 --> 00:04:49.310
three x squared.

00:04:50.055 --> 00:04:52.772
Now check v before you write its derivative.

00:04:53.376 --> 00:04:55.759
Sine two x has an inside, two x,

00:04:56.181 --> 00:04:57.923
so by the chain rule from last video,

00:04:58.265 --> 00:05:00.247
v prime is two cos two x.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:01.269
Then

00:05:01.792 --> 00:05:04.118
u prime v, plus u v prime, is

00:05:04.279 --> 00:05:06.986
three x squared sine two x, plus two

00:05:07.087 --> 00:05:08.591
x cubed cos two x.

00:05:09.333 --> 00:05:11.657
Both terms share x squared, so the answer

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:14.162
is x squared, times three sine two x,

00:05:14.303 --> 00:05:15.945
plus two x cos two x.

00:05:16.756 --> 00:05:18.002
Does that two matter?

00:05:18.708 --> 00:05:20.521
Check the slope at pi over two.

00:05:21.348 --> 00:05:24.303
There, sine pi is zero, and cos pi

00:05:24.445 --> 00:05:25.269
is minus one.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.131
So the first term vanishes, and the slope

00:05:28.172 --> 00:05:30.893
is two, times pi over two cubed, times

00:05:31.014 --> 00:05:31.614
minus one.

00:05:32.476 --> 00:05:34.480
That's minus pi cubed over four,

00:05:35.002 --> 00:05:36.885
about minus seven point seven five,

00:05:37.527 --> 00:05:38.688
and the tangent agrees.

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.521
Leave out the two, and you'd get half

00:05:41.582 --> 00:05:43.831
of that, a tangent that's far too shallow.

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:45.441
Here's a way to remember it.

00:05:46.024 --> 00:05:48.077
Each factor takes a turn, and the other

00:05:48.178 --> 00:05:48.721
one stays.

00:05:49.464 --> 00:05:51.649
In the rectangle, the width changes while the

00:05:51.709 --> 00:05:54.376
height stays, then the height changes while the

00:05:54.416 --> 00:05:54.977
width stays.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:57.810
That's why there are two terms, and why

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:00.281
each term keeps one of the original factors.

00:06:01.125 --> 00:06:03.932
Multiplying the two derivatives keeps neither factor, so

00:06:03.953 --> 00:06:04.775
it isn't the rule.

00:06:05.538 --> 00:06:07.427
And because the two turns are added, it

00:06:07.447 --> 00:06:08.954
doesn't matter which factor you call u.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:11.295
That won't be true for a quotient.

00:06:13.917 --> 00:06:14.365
Your turn.

00:06:14.975 --> 00:06:17.525
Differentiate f of x equals x squared e

00:06:17.566 --> 00:06:19.593
to the x, and give your answer fully

00:06:19.634 --> 00:06:20.176
factorised.

00:06:20.699 --> 00:06:21.484
Pause here to answer.

00:06:33.049 --> 00:06:35.663
u is x squared, so u prime is

00:06:35.764 --> 00:06:36.226
two x.

00:06:36.971 --> 00:06:38.956
v is e to the x, and so

00:06:39.038 --> 00:06:39.679
is v prime.

00:06:40.502 --> 00:06:42.443
So f prime of x is two x

00:06:42.584 --> 00:06:44.665
e to the x, plus x squared e

00:06:44.726 --> 00:06:45.125
to the x.

00:06:46.127 --> 00:06:48.108
Both terms share x e to the x,

00:06:48.569 --> 00:06:50.369
so f prime of x is x e

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:52.351
to the x, times x plus two.

00:06:53.274 --> 00:06:55.679
Multiplying the derivatives gives just two x e

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:57.945
to the x, which loses the second turn.

00:06:59.711 --> 00:07:00.114
Last one.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.607
Find the exact gradient of the curve y

00:07:03.749 --> 00:07:05.995
equals x e to the minus x,

00:07:06.537 --> 00:07:07.760
at x equals two.

00:07:08.547 --> 00:07:09.359
Pause here to answer.

00:07:20.237 --> 00:07:22.772
u is x, so u prime is one.

00:07:23.336 --> 00:07:25.640
v is e to the minus x, which

00:07:25.701 --> 00:07:28.546
has an inside, minus x, so v prime

00:07:28.808 --> 00:07:30.710
is minus e to the minus x.

00:07:31.373 --> 00:07:33.637
So d y by d x factors to

00:07:34.119 --> 00:07:36.523
e to the minus x, times one minus

00:07:36.665 --> 00:07:36.764
x.

00:07:37.546 --> 00:07:40.211
At x equals two, that's minus e to

00:07:40.232 --> 00:07:40.933
the minus two,

00:07:41.435 --> 00:07:42.958
about minus point one three.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:45.745
Lose the minus from the inside, and you'd

00:07:45.766 --> 00:07:47.570
get a positive slope, but the curve is

00:07:47.631 --> 00:07:48.212
falling there.

00:07:49.881 --> 00:07:51.967
So in a product, each factor takes a

00:07:52.007 --> 00:07:53.532
turn, while the other one stays.

00:07:54.475 --> 00:07:56.586
Next, one function divided by another.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.259
Here's e to the x, over x plus

00:07:59.380 --> 00:07:59.520
one.

00:08:00.184 --> 00:08:01.760
There's a gap where the bottom is zero.

00:08:02.406 --> 00:08:04.938
So how does dividing change the slope?

00:08:07.621 --> 00:08:08.505
Here are the key notes.

00:08:09.027 --> 00:08:10.796
Pause the video if you need more time

00:08:10.816 --> 00:08:11.298
to copy them.
